  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "WIND ON THE HILL",
      "cn": "山上的风"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "No one can tell me, Nobody knows, Where the wind comes from, Where the wind goes.",
      "cn": "没有人能够告诉我， 也没有人会知晓， 风从哪里来， 风往哪里去。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "It's flying from somewhere As fast as it can, I couldn't keep up with it, Not if I ran.",
      "cn": "它从某个地方飞来， 尽力飞快地奔跑， 我赶不上它， 即使我奔跑。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "But if I stopped holding The {string} of my kite, It would blow with the wind For a day and a night.",
      "cn": "但如果我松开手， 不再紧握风筝线， 它将随风飘荡， 一天一夜。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "And then when I found it, {Wherever} it blew, I should know that the wind Had been going there too.",
      "cn": "后来当我找到它， 无论它飘向何方， 我会知道风， 也曾去过那里。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "So then I could tell them Where the wind goes ... But where the wind comes from Nobody knows.",
      "cn": "所以那时我就能告诉他们， 风去了哪里…… 但是风从哪里来， 没有人知道。"
    },
    {
      "num": "07",
      "en": "— A. A. Milne",
      "cn": "—— A. A. 米尔恩"
    },
    {
      "num": "08",
      "en": "DREAM",
      "cn": "梦想"
    },
    {
      "num": "09",
      "en": "Hold fast to dreams For if dreams die Life is a broken-winged bird That cannot fly.",
      "cn": "紧紧抓住梦想， 因为梦想一旦消逝， 生活就像断了翅膀的小鸟， 再也不能飞翔。"
    },
    {
      "num": "10",
      "en": "Hold fast to dreams For when dreams go Life is a {barren} field Frozen with snow.",
      "cn": "紧紧抓住梦想， 因为梦想一旦远去， 生活就像荒芜的田野， 冰封大地白雪茫茫。"
    },
    {
      "num": "11",
      "en": "— Langston Hughes",
      "cn": "—— 兰斯顿·休斯"
    },
    {
      "num": "12",
      "en": "A MATCH",
      "cn": "佳偶"
    },
    {
      "num": "13",
      "en": "If love were what the rose is, And I were like the leaf, Our lives would grow together In sad or singing weather, Blown fields or flowerful closes, Green pleasure or gray {grief}; If love were what the rose is, And I were like the leaf.",
      "cn": "如果爱情好似香艳的玫瑰， 而我好似它的叶片青翠， 我们的生命将在一起生长， 无论天气阴沉或晴朗， 处在荒芜的原野，或花径， 感受绿色的欢乐，或灰色的悲愁； 如果爱情好似香艳的玫瑰， 而我好似它的叶片青翠。"
    },
    {
      "num": "14",
      "en": "— A. C. Swinburne",
      "cn": "—— A. C. 斯温伯恩"
    },
    {
      "num": "15",
      "en": "The poem Dream by Langston Hughes is very short with only 8 lines. When I read the poem aloud I can hear that the ends of the second and fourth sentences {rhyme} — \"die\" and \"fly\". The last word from the sixth and eighth sentences also {rhyme} — \"go\" and \"snow\". These rhyming words sound nice and make the poem pleasing to read.",
      "cn": "兰斯顿·休斯的诗作《梦想》非常短，只有8行。当我大声朗读这首诗时，我能听到第二句和第四句末尾押韵——\"die\"和\"fly\"。第六句和第八句的最后一个词也押韵——\"go\"和\"snow\"。这些押韵词听起来很悦耳，使诗歌读起来令人愉悦。"
    },
    {
      "num": "16",
      "en": "When I close my eyes, I can see different images from the poem. For example, I can see two hands being held. I can see a bird flying in the sky. I can see a field and I can imagine what it looks like with lots of snow. I start to feel cold when I read these lines!",
      "cn": "当我闭上眼睛，我能从诗中看到不同的意象。例如，我能看到两只手紧紧握住。我能看到一只鸟在天空中飞翔。我能看到一片田野，我能想象白雪覆盖的田野是什么样子。读到这些诗句时，我开始感到寒冷！"
    },
    {
      "num": "17",
      "en": "I learnt a new phrase, \"hold fast\", which means to hold onto something. \"{Barren}\" is also a new word to me, which means empty.",
      "cn": "我学到了一个新短语\"hold fast\"，意思是紧紧握住。对我来说，\"barren\"也是一个新词，意思是空旷的、荒芜的。"
    },
    {
      "num": "18",
      "en": "I think the poet is giving us advice. He wants us to keep dreaming, because life is much better when we dream and have something to look forward to.",
      "cn": "我认为诗人是在给我们建议。他希望我们坚持梦想，因为当我们怀有梦想、有所期盼时，生活会变得更加美好。"
    }
  ],
